markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h1>Section 4: Regression, Start to Finish</h1>

<div style="display: inline-block; background-color: #E4E2F8; color: #1F1976; font-weight: bold; font-size: 13px; padding: 4px 12px; border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 12px;">Aligns to curriculum Lessons 5-7</div>

<p>This section prepares you to teach three curriculum lessons, one complete arc. Students build a regression model, learn to test whether it's actually any good, then confront the question that matters most: where did the data come from, and does that data represent who the model will actually be used on?</p>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><b>Curriculum Lesson 5:</b> Building Regression Models</div>
  <a href="PASTE_UNIT_2_LESSON_5_URL_HERE" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 5</a>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><b>Curriculum Lesson 6:</b> Testing Regression Models</div>
  <a href="PASTE_UNIT_2_LESSON_6_URL_HERE" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 6</a>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><b>Curriculum Lesson 7:</b> Selecting Data</div>
  <a href="PASTE_UNIT_2_LESSON_7_URL_HERE" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 7</a>
</div>

<hr>

<p><b>In this section, you'll:</b></p>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; Build a linear regression model yourself, slope, y-intercept, the prediction line</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; Learn to measure how good a model actually is, using loss, not just "does it look right"</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; Get ahead of a real misconception: a model with fewer exact matches can still be the better model overall</div>
<div style="font-size: 16px;">&bull; Confront bias and representativeness in training data, using Anita's Parlor as the running example of what can go wrong</div>

<div style="background-color: #E4E2F8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #222222; line-height: 1.5;"><b>&#128161; Notice as you explore:</b> this is the first time the unit asks "is this model good?" rather than just "does this model work?" That distinction runs through all three lessons here.</div>
</div>

<hr>

